624 0 obj
  << /ActualText (1\056 The experience is efficient\054 but very administrative\056\nThe platform clearly focuses on submitting requests\054 passing them through approval steps\054 notifying stakeholders\054 and generating reports\056 That is useful for operations\054 but it can make the experience feel like a system for processing absences rather than helping people confidently plan time away\056\240\n\n2\056 Complexity grows quickly behind the scenes\056\nThe manual shows detailed settings for approval flows\054 substitutes\054 extra notifications\054 request rules\054 templates\054 and different absence types\056 This level of flexibility is powerful\054 but it can also create friction for first\055time users\054 managers\054 or admins who need to understand many rules before they feel in control\056\240\n\n3\056 Calendar readability can become overloaded\056\nThe calendar uses full fills\054 edge colors\054 legends\054 hover states\054 and multiple visual markers to show personal leave\054 sick leave\054 and colleagues\031 absences\056 In small teams this may work well\054 but in larger teams or busy periods it can become harder to scan quickly and understand at a glance\056 This is an interface\055design inference based on the documented calendar behavior\056\240\n\n4\056 Different user roles create competing needs\056\nThe product serves employees\054 managers\054 HR\054 finance\054 and leadership\054 each with different goals\056 Employees want speed and clarity\054 managers want team visibility\054 and HR\057payroll want reports and control\056 TIMEOFF\056GURU supports all of these\054 but combining them in one system increases the risk of dense navigation and feature\055heavy screens\056 This is an inference from the role\055specific feature set described on the site\056\240\n\n5\056 The system prioritizes control and reporting more than planning confidence\056\nReports are extensive\054 including status\054 type\054 location\054 sick leave\054 absenteeism\054 approval timing\054 and detailed exports\056 That makes the product strong for administration\054 but it suggests an opportunity to improve the emotional side of planning time off\072 helping users feel reassured\054 informed\054 and aware of team context before they submit a request\056 This is also an inference from the public feature emphasis\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 625 0 R
     /Pg 614 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

